    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "body": "## Bug\n\nImporting a local folder that is **already registered** as a project dead-ends the Import project modal: it shows the raw daemon error `A project at this path is already registered (PATH_ALREADY_REGISTERED)` with only *\"Choose a different folder to try again\"* + **Cancel**. There is no path to the already-registered project, even though the daemon tells the client exactly which project it is.\n\nReporter's ask: instead of this error, offer an option to **go to that project**.\n\n**Source:** Discord `#bug-triage` (2026-08-25)\n**Reported by:** @maaz\n**Analyzed against:** `origin/main` @ `4c3f4d72e`\n**Confidence:** High \u2014 full chain traced end-to-end (daemon \u2192 envelope \u2192 apiClient \u2192 CreateProjectFlow)\n**Priority:** medium \u2014 degraded UX, workaround exists (find the project manually in the sidebar)\n\n## Reproduction\n\n1. Have a project registered at path `P` (it is in the sidebar)\n2. `+` \u2192 **Import project** \u2192 *Choose a project folder* \u2192 select `P` in the OS picker\n3. Confirm creation in the agent sheet\n4. Daemon returns `409 PATH_ALREADY_REGISTERED`\n5. Modal re-opens in the bare folder-picker state: red error box with the raw message, footer *\"Choose a different folder to try again\"*, only **Cancel** available \u2014 a dead end\n\n![Import project modal showing the PATH_ALREADY_REGISTERED dead-end](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/i-trytoohard/codex-startup-factory/issue-assets-import-registered-deadend/.issue-assets/import-registered-deadend/modal.png)\n\n## Root Cause\n\nThe daemon already returns everything needed to recover \u2014 the renderer discards it at every layer.\n\n**The daemon side is fine:**\n\n- `backend/internal/service/project/service.go:196-200` \u2014 `Add()` returns `apierr.Conflict(\"PATH_ALREADY_REGISTERED\", \"A project at this path is already registered\", map[string]any{\"existingProjectId\": existing.ID, \"suggestedProjectId\": ...})`\n- `backend/internal/httpd/envelope/envelope.go:44` \u2014 `Details map[string]any json:\"details,omitempty\"` \u2014 so `details.existingProjectId` **is on the wire** in the 409 response.\n\n**Where the renderer drops it:**\n\n1. `frontend/src/renderer/routes/_shell.tsx` (`createProject`, ~L424-432):\n   ```ts\n   const failure = new Error(apiErrorMessage(error)) as Error & { code?: string };\n   failure.code = apiErrorCode(error);\n   throw failure;\n   ```\n   Only `message` + `code` survive. `error.details` \u2014 which carries `existingProjectId` \u2014 is dropped on the floor. There is no `apiErrorDetails()` helper at all (`frontend/src/renderer/lib/api-client.ts` has `apiErrorMessage` / `apiErrorCode` / `apiErrorRequestId` only).\n\n2. `frontend/src/renderer/lib/api-client.ts` (`apiErrorMessage`) renders `` `${body.message} (${code})` `` \u2014 which is exactly the `(PATH_ALREADY_REGISTERED)` suffix visible in the screenshot. Raw daemon code leaked into UI copy.\n\n3. `frontend/src/renderer/components/CreateProjectFlow.tsx:212-235` (`createProject` catch): `code` **is** extracted (line 213) but is only branched on for `NOT_A_GIT_REPO` / `PROJECT_UNBORN` repository-setup recovery. There is no branch for `PATH_ALREADY_REGISTERED` / `ID_ALREADY_REGISTERED`. So: `setError(message)`, and since `shouldScanCreateFailure()` (line 421-426) *explicitly returns `false`* for `(PATH|ID)_ALREADY_REGISTERED`, `validationScan` stays `null` \u2192 `CreateProjectFolderDialog` renders the bare dashed picker + error box + footer `createProject.footerChoose` (\"Choose a different folder to try again\", `en.json:166`).\n\n4. Pre-flight doesn't help either: the folder scan (`frontend/src/main/import-folder-scan.ts`, `scanGitRepo`) only knows git facts (bare, unborn, no remote, reserved name). It has no access to AO's registered-project list, so the user learns about the conflict only **after** confirming.\n\n## Fix\n\n1. **Carry the conflict payload**: in `_shell.tsx` `createProject` (and `cloneProject` for symmetry), attach `error.details` (or minimally `existingProjectId`) to the thrown error, e.g. add an `apiErrorDetails(error)` helper in `api-client.ts` next to the existing ones.\n2. **Branch on the code** in `CreateProjectFlow`'s catch: for `PATH_ALREADY_REGISTERED`, render a dedicated state in `CreateProjectFolderDialog` \u2014 \"This folder is already registered as a project\" with a primary **Go to project** action (navigate to `existingProjectId` via the existing project navigation; the project is already in the sidebar) and secondary *Choose a different folder*. Same pattern applies to `ID_ALREADY_REGISTERED`.\n3. **Optional belt-and-braces**: during the folder scan, flag the selected repo as \"already registered\" (the renderer already has the workspace/project list) so the user finds out at picker time, before confirming.\n\n## Impact\n\n- Any user who re-imports a folder that's already registered (new machine, restored disk, or simply forgetting it's in the long sidebar list) hits a hard dead-end that reads like a system fault rather than guidance.\n- The error copy exposes the raw daemon code (`PATH_ALREADY_REGISTERED`) verbatim, inconsistent with the rest of the import flow's human-readable messaging.\n\n## Related\n\n- #2721 \u2014 same flow, non-Git/nested import error messaging (different failure class, same \"raw error in modal\" shape)\n",
